## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/statisticsbyid.html
- Summary (EN): Statistics by ID computes statistics for the pixels of a Mono source layer, grouped by connected ID islands in an id layer. It reports each island's area, minimum and maximum values.
- Résumé (FR) : Statistics by ID calcule, pour chaque îlot connexe d'un calque ID, son aire ainsi que les valeurs minimale et maximale du calque source.

- Inputs meaning: ["id: ID layer, each connected component is treated as a separate statistics source", "source: Mono layer whose pixel values are measured"]

- Key parameters: ["No parameters are documented on the page (the Parameters section is empty)", "area: Mono layer giving the area of the island each pixel belongs to, in image units", "minimum: Mono layer giving the lowest source value within each pixel's island", "maximum: Mono layer giving the highest source value within each pixel's island"]

- Caveats: ["The page documents no parameters, check settings in Houdini itself", "Area is reported in image units, not pixel counts"]

